BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.78 Tm (The most expensive trap is the insurance gap. Etienne Elsaesser lays it out: platform commercial coverage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 222.55 Tm (only applies while the driver is logged in, on-trip third-party liability through Hugo only pays when the renter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 207.33 Tm (hits someone else, and a $4K car totaled in week one gets eaten by the owner because the deposit will) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 192.10 Tm (never cover it, a blind spot most operators only learn the hard way [amfsF8yd5hg @ 00:04:22].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.88 Tm (RevHostHQ's 'Sam' scenario shows the same hole from the compliance side: a cash handshake with a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 161.65 Tm (driver risks deactivation and leaves the car uninsured, so the fix is an approved route, a card on file, a check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 146.43 Tm (of the driver's insurance, and a weekly inspection [3jfvZ2LM8zM @ 00:01:26]. Even Kell King, who) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 131.20 Tm (self-insures and leans on a commercial liability policy for street compliance, concedes under questioning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.98 Tm (that the commercial policy is typically not going to pay out when an uninsured renter causes the loss) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.75 Tm ([5liDEdRcRhY @ 00:44:12]. The Kel King channel adds hard lines of its own: never run these cars on a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 85.53 Tm (personal policy, pair GPS with a kill switch, and back every handoff with a signed agreement and a deposit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 70.30 Tm (while checking local rules such as California smog testing [swveqE_MJY0 @ 00:07:23].) Tj ET
